    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0728" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3584</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Langhorne</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-31T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>462. Your 798, March 23, 4 p.m. It is assumed by this Government that the
                    position of the Dutch Government has no reference to the armed vessels of
                    neutral countries which may enter Dutch ports as ships of commerce. This
                    Government would be pleased to have this view confirmed by the Government of the
                    Netherlands.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
